---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import CrossLinks from '../components/CrossLinks.astro';
import Needs from '../components/Needs.astro';
import Draft from '../components/Draft.astro';
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="Choosing a model is a design decision with money attached"
  metaTitle="Word web — model evaluation study | Tyler Young"
  eyebrow="Shipped Product"
  current="building"
  meta={[
    ['Contribution', 'Designed, built and shipped with a two-person team'],
    ['Role', 'Design and product · live business'],
    ['Scope', 'Product design, model evaluation, production decision'],
    ['Evaluated', 'Twelve models · July 2026'],
    ['Live', '[NEEDS: URL + decision to expose]'],
  ]}
>
  <div class="aside">
    <p>
      Open decisions — the live URL, and the public framing. This is presented as a
      product and a business, not as children's media. Tyler signs off on the framing
      before this page ships.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>
    <Draft>
      Word pages that compose themselves in front of the reader — streaming,
      cross-linked, generated on request. Launched as a new brand and business.
    </Draft>
  </p>
  <p>
    <Needs>Tyler confirms the public framing in his own words</Needs>
  </p>

  <h2>The design problem</h2>
  <p>
    <Needs>
      Tyler's take — 2–3 sentences on designing for content that streams and composes
      live, where the page does not exist before the reader asks for it
    </Needs>
  </p>

  <h2>The model evaluation</h2>
  <p>
    <Draft>
      Twelve models, judged against the incumbent on four axes: quality, cost, latency
      and format conformance. Read by hand, not scored by another model.
    </Draft>
  </p>

  <div class="matrix-slot">
    <Needs block ratio="16 / 9">
      The evaluation matrix — table or image, sanitized to Tyler's comfort level.
      Model names in or out is his call.
    </Needs>
  </div>

  <h3>The decision</h3>
  <p>
    <Draft>
      Hands-on reading preferred the incumbent's coverage and overall quality. Several
      models matched it closely enough on paper, and lost on responsiveness — a page
      that composes in front of you cannot pause to think. The final call was a
      three-way trade between price, responsiveness and creative quality, and it
      resolved toward quality.
    </Draft>
  </p>

  <h3>Why it's on this site</h3>
  <p>
    <Draft>
      Model selection is a design decision. It sets the tempo of the interface, the
      texture of the writing, and the unit economics of the business, and it is made
      once and lived with. Putting it in a portfolio is only unusual because most
      design work never had a per-request cost attached.
    </Draft>
  </p>

  <div class="aside">
    <p>
      Not published, by design: prompts, evaluation criteria detail, and content
      frameworks. Competitive material for a live business.
    </p>
  </div>

  <CrossLinks
    slot="after"
    label="Related"
    title="The system behind this"
    links={[
      { href: '/how-i-design-with-ai', label: 'How I design with AI' },
      {
        href: '/atheer-design-pipeline',
        label: 'The design-to-code pipeline this came out of',
      },
    ]}
  />
</DocumentLayout>

<style>
  .matrix-slot {
    margin: 0 0 26px;
  }
</style>
